From 27ce067b0851df47067da74fad3ac5f1b6de821c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vishal Kumar Swain <vkswain50@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:11:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] neurosym: recognize textual true/false in local_eval_bool
 SYMBOL case

Investigated the reported gap where sign_extend/zero_extend composite
expressions supposedly fall through local_eval_bv() to the external
--neurosym-model-prog fallback. Traced a real run with temporary
instrumentation (removed before this commit):

smtlib_convt::mk_sign_ext()/mk_zero_ext() (inherited unchanged by
neurosym_convt, which does not override them) already lower both into
a CONCAT of the operand with either a zero bitvector (zero_extend) or
an ITE-selected all-zero/all-one prefix keyed on an EXTRACTed top bit
compared by EQ against 0 (sign_extend). Every node kind that lowering
produces -- CONCAT, EXTRACT, ITE, EQ, and BVINT constants -- is already
handled by local_eval_bv()/local_eval_bool(). A forced runtime trace
(inline (int)c / (unsigned int)c casts on a nondet char, verified with
diagnostic logging on the CONCAT/EXTRACT cases and on every fallthrough
default:) confirms this directly: both cases are evaluated fully
locally, with zero fallthrough to the default: case, and produce
values identical to the --neurosym-model-prog "z3 -in" fallback across
six additional differential tests spanning int8/uint8/int16/uint16
sign_extend and zero_extend, both positive and negative. So the
sign_extend/zero_extend gap does not exist in local_eval_bv/bool as
currently written; no change was needed there.

While forcing that runtime trace, a real, separate, and more
fundamental gap surfaced: local_eval_bool()'s SYMBOL case calls
local_lookup(), which only accepts numeric text via numeric_value().
A genuinely Bool-sorted local_model entry is stored as the literal text
"true"/"false" (as NeuroSym's own define-fun output and
parse_model_block() emit it), so local_lookup() always missed it and
local_eval_bool() fell through to nullopt for any boolean symbol -- in
particular the internal execution-state/guard booleans
(execution_statet::/bguard_exec?...) that appear in essentially every
non-trivial VCC via IMPLIES/NOT. That silently forced every multi-VCC
program (confirmed on test.c and div_test.c, not just contrived cases)
out to --neurosym-model-prog for its entire trace, even though every
other symbol involved was otherwise fully resolvable locally.

Fix: handle the textual true/false form directly in the SYMBOL case
before falling back to local_lookup()'s numeric-only parse, mirroring
how l_get() already special-cases these two strings for a direct
top-level symbol lookup.

Validated: clean rebuild; test.c and div_test.c now build their full
counterexample trace with --neurosym alone (no --neurosym-model-prog
at all), byte-identical (modulo timing/PID/tmpfile-name noise) to the
same runs with --neurosym-model-prog "z3 -in"; 6 differential
sign_extend/zero_extend tests (int8/uint8/int16/uint16, positive and
negative) pass with numerically correct values, identical between the
local and z3-fallback paths in every case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/solvers/neurosym/neurosym_conv.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/solvers/neurosym/neurosym_conv.cpp b/src/solvers/neurosym/neurosym_conv.cpp
index 9b7269dec7..2311787a35 100644
--- a/src/solvers/neurosym/neurosym_conv.cpp
+++ b/src/solvers/neurosym/neurosym_conv.cpp
@@ -496,6 +496,19 @@ std::optional<bool> neurosym_convt::local_eval_bool(smt_astt a) const
 
   case SMT_FUNC_SYMBOL:
   {
+    // local_lookup() only understands numeric text; a genuinely Bool-sorted
+    // model entry is textual ("true"/"false"), as NeuroSym's own
+    // define-fun output and parse_model_block() emit it -- handle that form
+    // directly here rather than failing through local_lookup()'s numeric
+    // parse and forcing every boolean-guarded trace out to the external
+    // fallback solver.
+    auto it = local_model.find(ast->symname);
+    if (it == local_model.end())
+      return std::nullopt;
+    if (it->second == "true")
+      return true;
+    if (it->second == "false")
+      return false;
     auto v = local_lookup(ast->symname);
     if (!v)
       return std::nullopt;
